## Why This Is Asked
Tests hands-on understanding of low-level memory management under contention: lock-free design, ABA-free reclamation, and NUMA-aware locality.

## Key Concepts
- Hazard pointers or epoch-based reclamation for UAF
- Size-class free lists and per-thread caches
- ABA avoidance in lock-free paths
- CAS-based global pool refills
- NUMA locality and cache-line alignment to minimize false sharing

## Code Example
